  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="Tag1017" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;!--?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?--&gt;
&lt;div style="line-height: 108%; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;
&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Chandeleur Pipe Line Company&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Notes to the Financial Statements&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Years Ended December 31, 2025 and 2024&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '1'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.49pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;1.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 9.49pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;The Company&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Chandeleur Pipe Line Company, LLC ("Chandeleur"), a wholly owned subsidiary of Third Coast Infrastructure, LLC ("TCI"), is an open-access interstate pipeline organized in May 1963. Chandeleur extends from federal offshore waters and runs through Louisiana, Alabama, and Mississippi state waters to onshore Mississippi and Alabama.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Chandeleur is engaged in interstate commerce and, as such, is subject to the rules, regulations and accounting procedures of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission, (the "FERC") pursuant to the Natural Gas Act of 1938 and the Natural Gas Policy Act of 1978.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '2'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.49pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;2.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 9.49pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Summary of Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements prescribed by the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("GAAP").&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The most significant difference between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein is that the FERC does not permit "push down" accounting for acquisitions.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Additionally, the FERC requires that the Company reflect a hypothetical provision for federal and state income taxes and related balance sheet accounts, even though it is not subject to such taxes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The preparation of the accompanying financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets, liabilities, revenues and expenses and the disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities that exist at the date of the financial statements.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Cash Management Program&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Chandeleur participates in a cash management program which is administered by TCI.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Chandeleur does not have its own bank account.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Cash is received and disbursed by TCI on behalf of Chandeleur and the net cash activity during the reporting period is reflected on the cash flow statement in financing activities as Intercompany Equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Transportation and Exchange Gas Imbalances&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;In the course of providing transportation services, natural gas pipelines may receive different quantities of gas from shippers than the quantities delivered on behalf of those shippers.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;These transactions result in transportation and exchange gas imbalances.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Such shipper imbalances are recorded as Regulatory Assets or Regulatory Liabilities in the accompanying balance sheet using the posted index prices of the applicable approved tariffs, which approximate market rates.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;These imbalances are required to be resolved within a specified period of time or when certain quantity thresholds are met.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Resolution can be through imbalance trading with other shippers or by utilizing the cash out procedures specified in the tariff.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Exchange imbalances are settled with other pipelines through the cashout procedures in their tariffs and recorded to the statement of income as Operating Expenses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Allowance for Doubtful Accounts&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Chandeleur establishes an allowance for losses on specific accounts receivable, as well as for gas imbalances due from shippers and operators, if collectability of such amounts is uncertain.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Collectability is reviewed periodically and the allowance is adjusted as necessary.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Chandeleur had no allowance for doubtful accounts as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '2'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.49pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Concentration of Credit Risk&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Concentrations of credit risk with respect to trade receivables are limited due to ongoing credit evaluations of customers.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;As of December 31, 2025, one customer had an accounts receivable balance in excess of 10% of our accounts receivable, net.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;This customer represented 100% of our outstanding accounts receivable as of December 31, 2025.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Significant customers are defined as those who represent 10% or more of the revenues during the year.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;For the year ended December 31, 2025, we had two customers which accounted for 100% of Chandeleur's revenues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Utility Plant&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Additions to utility plant are recorded at cost.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Major improvements are capitalized while routine maintenance and repairs are expensed as incurred.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;All dispositions or retirements are removed from property accounts at cost and such amounts, plus removal costs less salvage are charged to accumulated depreciation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Depreciation of utility plant assets is computed based on the 1.7% rate included in the approved tariff, plus negative salvage of 0.54% for mains.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The exception to this rate is the depreciation for the ARO asset which is 4.07% of the ARO asset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Impairment of Pipelines and Equipment&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Chandeleur reviews pipelines and equipment assets for impairment whenever events or changes in circumstances indicate that the carrying amount of an asset may not be recoverable.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;When it becomes probable that all or a portion of any pipelines and equipment assets will be disallowed for rate-making purposes, such amounts are deducted from the reported cost of the asset.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;There were no impairments in 2025 or 2024.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Chandeleur is not subject to federal or state income taxes; however, the related tax impacts of its operations are reported on the tax returns of the Chandeleur&amp;#8217;s sole member. For ratemaking purposes, Chandeleur is treated as if it were a corporation that would require comprehensive income tax procedures.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;In accordance with FERC requirements, the accompanying financial statements include a hypothetical provision for federal and state income taxes as if Chandeleur were a taxable entity following the guidance outlined in the Accounting Standards Codification 740, Income Taxes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Deferred tax assets and liabilities are recognized for the future tax consequences attributable to differences between the financial statement carrying amounts and the tax bases of existing assets and liabilities using enacted tax rates for the year in which the differences are expected to reverse.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;A valuation allowance is provided to offset deferred tax assets if, based upon the available evidence, it is more likely than not that some or all of the deferred tax assets will not be realized.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The current income tax provision for the year, which is reflected in Taxes Accrued on the balance sheet at year-end, will be relieved to Paid in Capital in the following year when the income tax returns are filed with the applicable tax authorities by the Company&amp;#8217;s sole member.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Allocation of Salary and Overhead Expense Policy&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;TCI allocates a portion of its corporate salaries and overhead to Chandeleur on the basis of the Modified Massachusetts Formula method based on a proportionate percentage of revenue, payroll costs and plant assets, which management believes to be reasonable in the circumstances.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Such allocation methods were consistently applied in 2025 and 2024 for values of $156,234 and $136,348, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Our interstate transportation results are determined primarily by the amount of capacity customers reserve as well as the actual volume of natural gas that flows through the transportation pipeline. Under transportation contracts, our customers are charged (i) a firm transportation fee, which is a fixed fee regardless of how much natural gas is transported, (ii) an annual charge adjustment unit fee, which is based on every unit of volume of natural gas delivered utilizing rates as determined by the FERC, (iii) an interruptible transportation fee if applicable, or (iv) a combination of the three.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Revenue is recognized over the service period specified in the contract as the services are rendered using a time-based (passage of time) or units-based (units of service transferred) method for measuring provision of the services. Progress towards satisfying our performance obligation is based on the firm or interruptible nature of the promised service and the terms and conditions of the contract.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Payment is generally received from the customer in the month of service or the month following the service. Contracts with customers generally are a combination of month-to-month and multi-year agreements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;In 2014, the Financial Accounting Standards Board (&amp;#8220;FASB&amp;#8221;) issued Accounting Standards Update (&amp;#8220;ASU&amp;#8221;) No. 2014-09, &amp;#8220;Revenue from Contracts with Customers (Topic 606)&amp;#8221;, which supersedes most of the existing revenue recognition requirements in GAAP and requires entities to recognize revenue at an amount that reflects the consideration to which an entity expects to be entitled in exchange for transferring goods or services to a customer. It also requires significantly expanded disclosures regarding the qualitative and quantitative information of an entity&amp;#8217;s nature, amount, timing and uncertainty of revenue and cash flows arising from contracts with customers.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;We are not adopting the new standard for FERC reporting purposes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Chandeleur follows Order No. 631, Accounting, Financial Reporting and Rate Filing Requirements for Asset Retirement Obligations ("ARO"), which addresses accounting and reporting for asset retirement obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived tangible assets.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Order No. 631 requires entities to record the fair value of a liability for the retirement obligation in the period in which the liability is incurred, if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The associated retirement cost is capitalized as part of the carrying value of the underlying asset and is subsequently depreciated over the underlying asset's useful life.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;After initial recognition, the ARO is revised to reflect the passage of time through accretion and for changes in the estimate amount or timing of cash flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Legal obligations exist for certain of the Company's right-of-way agreements due to requirements or landowner options to compel the Company to remove the pipe at the final abandonment. Effectively, an ARO was established in 2019 for this future abandonment responsibility and updated in 2025. See Note 7 for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Financial Instruments&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Chandeleur&amp;#8217;s financial instruments consist of accounts receivable and accounts payable.&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The carrying amount of these financial instruments represents their fair value based their short-term nature.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '3'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.65pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;3.&lt;font style="width: 9.65pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Utility Plant&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;Utility plant, net, as of December 31, 2025 and 2024 consisted of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
